    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>character_pointer</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when the type is a pointer to a <computeroutput>character</computeroutput>, possibly <computeroutput>const</computeroutput>, but not <computeroutput>volatile</computeroutput>. The formatter writes these pointers as C strings, and <computeroutput>located_name</computeroutput> takes them as names.</para>
